<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>All the news about Africa - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:01:48 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>Togo says it has 'serious' evidence against detained French journalists</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260823-togo-says-it-has-serious-evidence-against-detained-french-journalists</link><description>
Togo's government says it has "serious and consistent evidence" against two French documentary filmmakers detained since July on charges of making false statements. Gaël Mocaër and Sebastian Perez Pezzani were arrested along with their Togolese fixer, Fred Vedomey, and have denied wrongdoing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdddc9cc-9ec9-11f1-9875-e5f10da2b52b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 08:56:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg">© AFP/EMILE KOUTON</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>'An invisible avalanche': what happened in Cameroon's 1986 Lake Nyos disaster?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-an-invisible-avalanche-what-happened-in-cameroon-s-1986-lake-nyos-disaster</link><description>
On 21 August, 1986, 1,746 people died from carbon dioxide poisoning after gas escaped overnight from the bottom of Lake Nyos in Cameroon. RFI examines what happened in the world's deadliest "limnic eruption" and how, 40 years later, our understanding of the danger posed by volcanic lakes is still evolving. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6970f48a-1541-11ea-b2e0-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/lake_nyos_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6970f48a-1541-11ea-b2e0-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/lake_nyos_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f1af974-9d4c-11f1-8f6e-f35f06fd4b75</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:47:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6970f48a-1541-11ea-b2e0-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/lake_nyos_0.jpg">Wikipedia/Domaine public</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo Ebola outbreak 'growing exponentially' with more than 2,500 dead</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-dr-congo-ebola-outbreak-growing-exponentially-with-more-than-2-500-dead</link><description>
The Ebola outbreak raging in the Democratic Republic of Congo is growing "exponentially", with more than 2,500 deaths recorded and half of those in the last 20 days, the senior UN coordinator on the disease said Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">837f67ba-9d54-11f1-9288-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:36:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg">© Jospin Mwisha / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Cameroon’s President Biya home after 73-day absence, amid health speculation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-cameroon-president-biya-home-after-73-day-absence-amid-health-speculation</link><description>
Cameroon’s President Paul Biya has returned to the country after spending 73 days abroad, ending an unusually long absence that has intensified speculation around the 93-year-old’s health and raised questions over Cameroon's political future.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff0dfbf0-9d34-11f1-a29e-831a4ab27004</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:11:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg">AP - Sunday Alamba</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Deadly border mine collapse exposes risks behind Central Africa's gold rush</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260820-deadly-border-mine-collapse-exposes-risks-behind-central-africa-s-gold-rush-zamboye</link><description>
A deadly landslide at a gold mine on the Cameroon-Central African Republic border has triggered calls for greater oversight of mining operations, after dozens of people were killed and many more were reported missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa4723ae-7a99-11ef-9f4c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Gaga-mines-or.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa4723ae-7a99-11ef-9f4c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Gaga-mines-or.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49f67a2a-9c90-11f1-ab31-a5221940408f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:47:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa4723ae-7a99-11ef-9f4c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Gaga-mines-or.jpg">© RFI/Rolf Steve Domia-Leu</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Five years on from first vaccine, fight against malaria sees progress in Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260820-five-years-on-from-first-vaccine-fight-against-malaria-sees-progress-in-africa</link><description>
On World Mosquito Day, attention remains focused on the devastating impact of the disease in Africa. The continent accounts for 95 per cent of malaria-related deaths worldwide. Five years after the roll-out of the first malaria vaccine, it is beginning to deliver measurable results – although significant challenges remain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b09af880-9c6f-11f1-a353-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25230427734255.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b09af880-9c6f-11f1-a353-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25230427734255.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e5f87ce-9c92-11f1-bc8c-81338d49049e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:23:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b09af880-9c6f-11f1-a353-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25230427734255.jpg">© AP - Patrick Onen</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rights group calls for release of two French journalists held in Togo</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260820-rights-group-calls-for-release-of-two-french-journalists-held-in-togo-ga%C3%ABl-moca%C3%ABr-sebastian-perez-pezzani</link><description>
Two French journalists detained in Togo since late July have been placed in pre-trial detention and charged with "false statements", Reporters Without Borders (RSF) has said, calling for their immediate release. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/256d789e-68cb-11ee-ba4d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Chu_%281%29.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/256d789e-68cb-11ee-ba4d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Chu_%281%29.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e36a440-9c75-11f1-a3a4-815bbe2c6f6d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:19:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/256d789e-68cb-11ee-ba4d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Chu_%281%29.jpg">© Theolebaron/WikiCommons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Twenty years after Probo Koala, Africa still grapples with ‘waste colonialism’</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260819-twenty-years-after-probo-koala-africa-still-grapples-with-waste-colonialism-abidjan</link><description>
Twenty years after toxic waste from the cargo ship Probo Koala was dumped across Abidjan in Côte d'Ivoire, the disaster remains an open wound for many victims and a symbol of wealthy countries sending unwanted waste to Africa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7ab2f0c-9b81-11f1-aa59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par942011.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7ab2f0c-9b81-11f1-aa59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par942011.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">078fe796-9ba2-11f1-acad-6748bf4168d5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:02:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7ab2f0c-9b81-11f1-aa59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par942011.jpg">AFP - RAIGO PAJULA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Liberia to take in up to 1,200 US deportees within a year</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260819-liberia-to-take-in-up-to-1-200-us-deportees-within-a-year</link><description>
Liberia has announced it will receive up to 1,200 foreign nationals deported from the United States – one of the largest known deals struck with African countries as part of President Donald Trump's unprecedented bid to drive out undocumented migrants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4604c40-f77f-11f0-a0a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-923W4W2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4604c40-f77f-11f0-a0a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-923W4W2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b27abf02-9bbe-11f1-995b-7bd032427e98</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:44:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4604c40-f77f-11f0-a0a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-923W4W2.jpg">AFP - OCTAVIO JONES</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigeria election campaign begins as voters grapple with inflation crisis</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260819-nigeria-election-campaign-begins-as-voters-grapple-with-inflation-crisis</link><description>
Campaigning kicks off in Nigeria Wednesday, five months ahead of elections set to be dominated by crushing inflation and President Bola Tinubu's economic reforms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2fc00424-9b90-11f1-b0a8-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/7e69cc975f78e6d3417eaa105cdddfc75772fef7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2fc00424-9b90-11f1-b0a8-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/7e69cc975f78e6d3417eaa105cdddfc75772fef7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">311cfe94-9b90-11f1-b24c-e139435d64a2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 05:38:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2fc00424-9b90-11f1-b0a8-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/7e69cc975f78e6d3417eaa105cdddfc75772fef7.jpg">© Light Oriye Tamunotonye / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DRC authorities warn Ebola outbreak is worst to date and yet to peak</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260818-drc-authorities-warn-ebola-outbreak-is-worst-to-date-and-yet-to-peak</link><description>
The Democratic Republic of Congo’s latest Ebola outbreak has become the deadliest in the country’s history, surpassing the devastating 2018-2020 epidemic even as health authorities warn that the current outbreak is yet to reach its peak.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/efd68a3a-5d8d-11f1-afd8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-31T105324Z-1145257280-RC29KLAFNPUZ-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-WHO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/efd68a3a-5d8d-11f1-afd8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-31T105324Z-1145257280-RC29KLAFNPUZ-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-WHO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7546194-9ada-11f1-88e0-5b2668a9d0ce</guid><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:17:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/efd68a3a-5d8d-11f1-afd8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-31T105324Z-1145257280-RC29KLAFNPUZ-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-WHO.jpg">© REUTERS - Gradel Muyisa Mumbere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Hichilema secures second term after tense Zambia election</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260818-zambia-s-president-hichilema-wins-re-election</link><description>
Zambia's electoral commission has announced that Hakainde Hichilema has been re-elected president after a race that critics said was tightly managed by his government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa085f06-9aa0-11f1-adc6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225403948990.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa085f06-9aa0-11f1-adc6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225403948990.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b029ecfa-9ac4-11f1-ba58-050d7640fbe9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 05:21:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa085f06-9aa0-11f1-adc6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225403948990.jpg">© Anita Reed/AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Solar-powered community gardens offer lifeline in drought-hit Zimbabwe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260816-solar-powered-community-gardens-offer-lifeline-in-drought-hit-zimbabwe</link><description>
At a shared garden in eastern Zimbabwe, solar-powered pumps are helping farmers grow crops year round, even when drought dries out other fields. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9d4442e-97c7-11f1-a081-371e64013e18</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:53:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg">© Farai Shawn Matiashe</source><dc:creator>Farai Shawn Matiashe</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>US missionary kidnapped in Niger freed after more than nine months</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260814-us-missionary-kidnapped-in-niger-freed-after-more-than-nine-months-in-captivity</link><description>
American Kevin Rideout, who worked as a pilot for an evangelical organisation, has been freed after he was kidnapped in October 2025 in Niamey. His release comes as the security situation remains tense in Niger. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2159fc1a-6c5a-11f1-b030-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-19T041459Z-311690609-RC2RWLA8S6JE-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2159fc1a-6c5a-11f1-b030-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-19T041459Z-311690609-RC2RWLA8S6JE-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aaa8747c-97e0-11f1-9d1b-61ddff2f7428</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:22:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2159fc1a-6c5a-11f1-b030-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-19T041459Z-311690609-RC2RWLA8S6JE-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg">via REUTERS - ORTN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Zambia suspends vote counting nationwide citing violence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260814-zambia-suspends-vote-counting-nationwide-citing-violence</link><description>
Zambia suspended vote counting nationwide on Friday following reports of violence in some districts, the electoral commission said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71e94a7a-97d7-11f1-b790-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fde95d622020d705e303b29b9aa9f9eaa2522446.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71e94a7a-97d7-11f1-b790-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fde95d622020d705e303b29b9aa9f9eaa2522446.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72e811f4-97d7-11f1-8606-c132d391fb73</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:58:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71e94a7a-97d7-11f1-b790-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fde95d622020d705e303b29b9aa9f9eaa2522446.jpg">© GIANLUIGI GUERCIA / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Renewed fighting in Tigray raises risk of a wider regional war</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260814-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-raises-risk-of-a-wider-regional-war</link><description>
A recent flare-up in tensions in Ethiopia's Tigray, including reports of heavy artillery battles and drone strikes, has raised fears of a return to war in the northern state – a conflict potentially stoked by foreign nations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0761e16-9563-11f1-9e6e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ee6b62455937fba6d9ab1d92fad3ae3e33723a01-1.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0761e16-9563-11f1-9e6e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ee6b62455937fba6d9ab1d92fad3ae3e33723a01-1.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bed4bdc8-97c9-11f1-9948-371e64013e18</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:20:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0761e16-9563-11f1-9e6e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ee6b62455937fba6d9ab1d92fad3ae3e33723a01-1.jpeg">AFP - EDUARDO SOTERAS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Mali junta pardons French agent jailed for 'undermining state security'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260814-mali-junta-pardons-french-agent-jailed-for-undermining-state-security-yann-v%C3%A9zilier</link><description>
Mali's junta leader General Assimi Goïta has pardoned a French intelligence agent serving a 20-year prison sentence, a rare conciliatory move after years of strained relations between the west African nation and its former colonial ruler.    
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e88ba716-20ec-11f1-bfe7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Assimi-Goita-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e88ba716-20ec-11f1-bfe7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Assimi-Goita-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5822d170-97ae-11f1-9f60-573bc02574bf</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 08:25:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e88ba716-20ec-11f1-bfe7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Assimi-Goita-1.jpg">AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Voters in Zambia to deliver verdict on president's economic record</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260813-voters-in-zambia-to-deliver-verdict-on-president-s-economic-record</link><description>
Zambia are voting in a general election on Thursday which will decide whether President Hakainde Hichilema returns for a second term, after steering the country out of a debt crisis.
